---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base title="Resources — PerfEco Consulting" description="PerfEco blog: practical articles on organisational performance, executive management and digital transformation in New Caledonia.">
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-16">

    <section class="bg-navy-dark text-white py-20 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Resources</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">Insights for executives</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg">Practical articles on organisational performance, management and transformation — in the NC &amp; Pacific context.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-20 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="space-y-8">
          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Management</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 1/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">1 September 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">What a management rhythm actually is</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">The offsite, the action plan, the working group all mobilise people for a few weeks, then everything fades. What makes change stick is what comes back on a fixed date. The four markers of a real management rhythm, and where to start.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/building-a-management-rhythm-that-lasts" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>
          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Organisation</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 8/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">25 August 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Realigning the organisation behind the strategy</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">The final article of the series. Seven findings, one cause: the organisation is built to run, not to execute. The four alignments to fix — deciding, pacing, seeing, measuring — in that order.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/realigning-the-organisation-behind-the-strategy" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Steering</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 7/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">18 August 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">KPIs do not create performance</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Fewer than 25% of organisations achieve sustained performance improvement (McKinsey, 2026). Measuring is not steering: what creates performance is not the metric, but the decision it triggers.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/kpis-do-not-create-performance" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Executive Committee</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 6/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">11 August 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Executive committees often lack visibility</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">75% of executives say they don't trust the data they rely on to make decisions (Gartner, 2025). At every level of the hierarchy, information gets filtered, softened, and summarized before it ever reaches the boardroom.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/the-executive-committee-often-lacks-visibility" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Steering</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 5/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">4 August 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Meetings don't replace steering</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">An executive spends an average of 23 hours a week in meetings. A single weekly Executive Committee meeting can cascade into up to 300,000 hours of work a year. More meetings don't guarantee you're steering anything.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/meetings-dont-replace-steering" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Execution</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 4/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">28 July 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Why projects slow down — what really derails them</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">91.5% of megaprojects go over budget or over schedule. It's almost never a skills problem. 4 signals foreshadow a project that's about to slow down.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/why-projects-slow-down" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Governance</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Special edition</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">21 July 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Who really has the right to decide? The blind spot in executive committee governance</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">An org chart and a RACI matrix aren't enough to make decisions work. 4 recurring mistakes explain why the right people often don't actually hold the power to decide.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/who-really-has-the-right-to-decide" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Performance</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 3/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">15 July 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Wealth is not enough: what the highest-performing organisations understood</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Zurich, Singapore, Copenhagen: their real advantage isn't only financial — it's organisational. 4 levers separate high-performing organisations from the rest.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/wealth-is-not-enough" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Strategy</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 2/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">7 July 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Strategy alone is not enough: execution as a competitive advantage</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Harvard Business Review estimates that 40% of strategic value is lost at the execution stage. McKinsey confirms: healthy organisations are 3× more likely to outperform. The 4 pillars of rigorous execution.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/strategy-alone-is-not-enough" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Execution</span>
              <span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Series · 1/8</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">30 June 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Why strategic plans fail to deliver — even when the strategy is sound</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">A solid strategy is not enough. Execution is the rare and decisive competence. Symptoms, root causes and 4 levers to bridge strategy and concrete results in your organisation.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/why-strategic-plans-fail" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Governance</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">23 June 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Is a file still standard? The 3 criteria every manager must master</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">A file ceases to be standard as soon as it exceeds the usual framework in complexity, amount or risk. Three simple criteria that prevent costly misclassification.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/standard-file-escalation-criteria" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs bg-teal/10 text-teal font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Management</span>
              <time class="text-xs text-gray-400">18 June 2026</time>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3 leading-snug">Geopolitical volatility: 5 levers to turn it into a competitive advantage</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Instability has become structural. How can executive committees transform this constraint into an advantage? A PerfEco reading of McKinsey Quarterly research.</p>
            <a href="/en/resources/geopolitical-volatility-advantage" class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">Read the article →</a>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-14 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-8 text-center">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy mb-3">Receive future articles</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mb-6">Analysis and practical guides on executive performance in NC &amp; French Polynesia — no jargon, directly actionable.</p>
          <form name="newsletter-en" method="POST" data-netlify="true" class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 max-w-md mx-auto">
            <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="newsletter-en" />
            <input type="email" name="email" required placeholder="your@email.nc" class="flex-1 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg px-3 py-2.5 text-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-teal" />
            <button type="submit" class="bg-teal hover:bg-teal-dark text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg text-sm transition-colors">Subscribe</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
